# WHY: Internal maintainer artifacts. These are session handoffs, generated
# architecture maps, and review/audit reports that go stale on every commit and
# describe retired implementation details. They stay useful on a maintainer's
# machine but must not ship in a public repository.
HANDOFF.md
PORTING.md
PROJECT_MAP.md
REPORT.md
FIX-LOG.md

# WHY: Local agent workspaces and dead git worktrees. These are excluded by
# machine-local config only (.git/info/exclude and a per-user global ignore
# file), neither of which travels with the repository. Without these rules a
# different clone, or the same machine after that config is reset, would stage
# a full duplicate checkout plus absolute local paths and permission grants.
.claude/
.kilo/
.test-env-tmp/
